--You put the seasoned orc corpse onto the fire...

The mind boggles...

Seriously, what nethack could really use is a cauldron: It would be a
hugely heavy item, or maybe an immovable dungeon feature like an
altar. You'd want at least one guaranteed cauldron in the game, and
maybe a way to create one (wish? Polypile a big heap of iron?) Once
you find your cauldron and get a fire going under it, you could mix
potions in it for more controllable alchemy or even create potions
from raw ingredients. (Poisonous corpse + water= potion of sickness,
quantum mechanic corpse=potion of speed etc) With a gourmand patch,
you'd be able to boil food in there as well. Obviously you'd want lots
of unexpected balancing effects as well- nasties creeping out of them,
explosions, cauldrons falling off their supports and crushing feet
etc- but i can't be arsed to think of any now.

There could also be a magic cauldron- there are more than a few of
those in mythology- with special properties. For example Schrimnir was
a norse cauldron in Valhalla, which generated infinite booze. Also, I
believe celtic mythology (or at least, I remember from one of the
Slaine graphic novels=-) has a magic cauldron that can regenerate the
dead and also commune with the Gods (altar powers?)

